invariant reading
1. The naive three-tail comb frontier is dominated by packets that delete
   a shell-1 tower bit. HYP-2661 should remove those before exact tail
   enumeration; the broad comb was doing avoidable work.
2. After the shell-1 gate, the worst first-tail cutoff drops from the
   global frontier to the shell-1-full frontier. The remaining packets
   should be attacked by mouth survival / endpoint-owner addresses, not
   by replacement count alone.
3. This gives a proof-order recipe: tower conservation first, root packet
   second, nested comb finite residues third.

Tournament Analysis
  vertices: shell1_gate, root_packet, mouth_owner, nested_comb, raw_replacement_count
  observable: finite residue burden for proving meas(G_C)>=426/35035
  Hamiltonian path: shell1_gate > root_packet > mouth_owner > nested_comb > raw_replacement_count
  challenged assumption: the first AP-tail quotient is not the number of tails; it is whether the shell-1 carrier survives.
